From 24126ff929100213e77049a91f7d96bc0640db82 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Semih Baskan <strst.gs@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 23 Nov 2026 12:41:46 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] ARM: dts: BCM5301X: RT-N18U: drop the flow accelerator tag

Patch 379 names the prepended Broadcom tag on ports 5 and 8, so the
flow accelerator is in the path on every boot, whether hardware flow
offloading is on or not. Drop those lines and the port 8 node that
only carried one of them. The switch then boots with the regular tag,
and the bcm53xx preinit hook moves it to the prepended tag when the
firewall's flow offloading and hardware flow offloading are both on.

Port 5 stays a CPU port with its fixed link, for the switch's trap
rules. User ports keep port 8 as their CPU port.

Measured on an RT-N18U: with hardware flow offloading off the switch
kept the regular tag and the accelerator stayed out of the path; with
both options on the hook moved it to the prepended tag at boot and a
TCP stream ran through the accelerator at 949 Mbit/s.

Signed-off-by: Semih Baskan <strst.gs@gmail.com>
---
 arch/arm/boot/dts/broadcom/bcm47081-asus-rt-n18u.dts | 6 ------
 1 file changed, 6 deletions(-)

--- a/arch/arm/boot/dts/broadcom/bcm47081-asus-rt-n18u.dts
+++ b/arch/arm/boot/dts/broadcom/bcm47081-asus-rt-n18u.dts
@@ -137,8 +137,6 @@
 		};
 
 		port@5 {
-			dsa-tag-protocol = "brcm-prepend";
-
 			fixed-link {
 				speed = <1000>;
 				full-duplex;
@@ -148,9 +146,5 @@
 		port@7 {
 			status = "disabled";
 		};
-
-		port@8 {
-			dsa-tag-protocol = "brcm-prepend";
-		};
 	};
 };
